# Data conversion between byte and pebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between byte and pebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1B to 0.0000PiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5B yields 0.0000PiB; backward, converting 1PiB to 1125899906842624B preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5PiB yields 1688849860263936.0B. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1B
print(forward_whole->to(PiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(forward_fractional->to(PiB))
backward_whole: int = 1PiB
print(backward_whole->to(B))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PiB
print(backward_fractional->to(B))

<<< stdout
0.0000PiB
0.0000PiB
1125899906842624B
1688849860263936.0B

<<< stderr
